+# The run is split into jobs that each get their own machine, so the wall clock is the slowest job
+# rather than the sum of every step, and a machine never runs more than its share of compilers or
+# test workers at once.
+#
+# Memory is why the split matters as much as the speed. On a private repository `ubuntu-24.04` is
+# GitHub's standard runner: 2 vCPUs and about 7.9 GB. One job-wide NODE_OPTIONS heap applies to
+# every Node process at once, and V8 does not collect until a process nears its own limit, so a
+# large job-wide heap with three compilers running lets the machine run out of memory first; the
+# runner then stops answering ("The hosted runner lost communication with the server") and GitHub
+# gives up on it only much later. Each job below sets a per-process heap that its parallelism fits
+# into the machine (heap x parallelism + 1 GB stays under 7.9 GB): 2 GB at three at once, 3 GB at
+# two at once, more only for a process that is alone on its machine. Raise a heap only together
+# with a lower --parallel. Test runners start worker processes that inherit NODE_OPTIONS; the cap
+# bounds each one, and none comes near it in practice.
+#
+# The runner label comes from the CI_RUNNER repository variable (Settings > Secrets and variables >
+# Actions > Variables), so moving every job to another runner is a setting, not a workflow change.
+# Unset, it is GitHub's standard runner.
+#
+# Every Linux job starts from .github/actions/setup (pnpm, Node, install, Prisma client). Nx Cloud's
+# remote cache is shared across the jobs and across runs, so a task whose inputs are unchanged
+# replays in seconds wherever it is scheduled. This file is in nx.json's sharedGlobals, so a change
+# to it misses the cache everywhere once.
+env:
+  FORCE_JAVASCRIPT_ACTIONS_TO_NODE24: true
+  NX_DAEMON: false
+  # Nx Cloud remote cache, per Nx's recommendation: pushes to develop (a protected branch) use the
+  # read-write token; pull requests use the read-only token, which gives each PR its own scoped
+  # cache so PR code can never write into the cache develop trusts. A fork's PR gets no secrets
+  # and runs with the anonymous access the workspace allows (none).
+  NX_CLOUD_ACCESS_TOKEN: ${{ github.event_name == 'push' && secrets.NX_CLOUD_ACCESS_TOKEN || secrets.NX_CLOUD_ACCESS_TOKEN_READ }}
+  # The projects whose tests run in the `tests-web` job. Every other project's tests run in
+  # `tests-api`, which EXCLUDES this list rather than naming its own, so a new project's tests run
+  # there without anyone remembering to list it.
+  WEB_TEST_PROJECTS: web,web-ui,web-components,data-browser,shared-components,utils,apollo,sdk,access-control
